 * K3 implant · W5-T5 · four-level funnel (§4.4.4): candidate → regression set → holdout tasks →
 * promotion, monotone in risk exposure.
 *
 * COMPONENT TRIPLE
 * - Reason to exist : single-stage evaluation cannot distinguish "overfit to the gate suite"
 *                     from "actually generalises" (§4.4.10 row 3). Each level widens exposure
 *                     and reduces reversibility, so each level's criteria must be STRICTER and
 *                     its evidence MORE REAL than the previous one.
 * - Axiom binding   : Axiom 6 (statistics: non-parametric test + MDE + sample floors); Axiom 9
 *                     (the funnel IS the empirical adoption gate GAP-007 shows upstream lacks).
 * - Deprecation     : compressible to 2 levels only when per-eval cost drops below gate-管理
 *                     overhead (G2 clause, pure offline micro-benchmarks); the G16 disjointness
 *                     (search set ∩ acceptance set = ∅) is NOT deprecable.
 *
 * LEVELS (each with explicit pass/reject criteria; every verdict is a `cand.eval` ledger row):
 *   F0 admission   — deterministic L1 checks all green (compile/schema/lint/test), auto;
 *   F1 regression  — held-out golden regression green ∧ upstream anchors green ∧ no champion
 *                    regression;
 *   F2 holdout     — primary metric significantly better (Mann-Whitney U + MDE) ∧ guardrails
 *                    unbroken ∧ critical untriggered ∧ canary untriggered ∧ sample floor met;
 *                    every holdout evaluation is one `holdout.query` row (Thresholdout);
 *   F3 promotion   — F2 pass ∧ Refute-or-Promote survived ∧ G15 comparison rows complete ∧
 *                    dual-sign present; pass@k-only gains are RESAMPLING EFFECTS → RECYCLE.
 *
 * G11: a frozen FCQ stops the funnel at the F1|F2 boundary — F0/F1 still run (shadow
 * accumulation is allowed while frozen; the POINTER never moves), F2+ refuse (holdout budget is
 * itself an FCQ subquantity; spending it while the channel is unreliable is waste plus leak).
